Here’s a clean, generalized step-by-step version of that workflow you demonstrated. I’ve removed project-specific names and made it reusable for any approval-driven deployment pipeline.


---

End-to-End Approval & Deployment Workflow (General Guide)

1. Submit for Security Review

Navigate to the workflow stage labeled Security Review

Assign a reviewer (e.g., security team member)

Submit the review request

The reviewer receives an email notification with a link



---

2. Security Reviewer Actions

Open the email and follow the review link

Access the review page

Set Status = Approved (or Reject if needed)

Click Submit Review



---

3. Post-Security Approval

Requestor receives notification of approval

Open the workflow item via email or dashboard

Click Edit

Mark the stage as Finished

Click Save to unlock the next stage



---

4. Deployment Approval Request

Assign the next approver (e.g., deployment or engineering lead)

Send approval request

Approver receives email notification



---

5. Deployment Approval Actions

Approver opens email link

Reviews deployment details

Sets Status = Approved

Submits review



---

6. Deploy to Staging

After approval, enable deployment actions

Trigger:

Deploy with review flag (if applicable)

Deploy to staging environment


Confirm deployment status shows Approved / Successful



---

7. Verify Deployment

Check:

Deployment node / pipeline logs

Staging environment

Activated bundle/version


Ensure the correct version is deployed and active



---

8. Mark Stage Complete

Return to workflow

Set current stage as Finished

Save changes



---

9. Data Validation (Pre-Production)

Assign Data Scientist / Analyst for validation

Reviewer:

Reviews datasets

Validates outputs in staging

Provides sign-off approval




---

10. Final Approval for Production

After data validation:

Initiate production deployment approval

Typically handled by:

Advanced analytics team

Engineering lead

Change control board





---

11. Deploy to Production

Once all approvals are complete:

Execute production deployment

Follow change control procedures


Confirm deployment success



---

12. Completion

Workflow reaches final state

Project is live in production



---

Key Concepts Behind the Flow

Email-driven approvals ensure traceability

Stage locking/unlocking enforces order

Multiple sign-offs reduce risk

Staging validation prevents production issues

Separation of roles (security, deployment, data) improves reliability



